# {{.Name}}

A skit-based HTTP service scaffolded by `skit new --full`.

## Run locally

```bash
go mod tidy
docker compose up -d          # postgres (+ rabbitmq)
go run . migrate up
go run . serve                # :8080 GET /hello; localhost:6060 /healthz, /readyz, /metrics
```

Configuration is 12-factor: every flag has an env var (see `.env.example`).
Copy it to `.env` for local development.

## Run modes

The same binary runs as one process or as several, depending on the command:

| Command | Runs | Replicas |
|---|---|---|
| `serve` | API + workers + consumers | 1 (local dev, single pod) |
| `http` | API only | N |
| `worker` | background loops + outbox workers | 1 |
| `consumer` | queue consumers only | N |

A command is a list of options (`internal/app/server/options.go`), e.g. `worker`:

```go
return run(c.ServerOpts,
	server.WithServer(c.Debug.Addr, server.Debug),
	server.WithWorkers(),
)
```

`WithServer(addr, route sets…)` adds an HTTP server; an empty address adds none,
so clearing `HTTP_ADDR` or `DEBUG_ADDR` turns that server off. `Install` is the
business API with its request middleware chain; `Debug` is the technical sets —
`Health` (`/healthz`, `/readyz`), `Metrics`, `Pprof`, `Info` (`/debug/components`).
Every command serves `Debug` on `DEBUG_ADDR`, so the probes work in every process —
point the Kubernetes probes there and the same manifest fits every pod. In a
container set `DEBUG_ADDR=:6060`; the default `localhost:6060` is not reachable by
the kubelet. To put a set on another port, edit the command's list.

`GET /debug/components` reports what the process runs — the same values it logs
at startup: `{"servers":[":8080","localhost:6060"],"workers":0,"consumers":0}`.

A wall-clock cron in the worker process fires once per replica — keep the worker at
one replica or gate the job with a `lock.Locker` (`skit add cron --lock`).

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `internal/cmd` | `serve` / `http` / `worker` / `consumer` / `migrate` / `version` subcommands (go-flags) |
| `internal/app/config` | configuration: one struct → flags + env + `--help` |
| `internal/app/deps` | lazy dependency container + ordered initializers |
| `internal/app/server` | options the commands compose (servers, route sets, workers, consumers), business routes (`Install`) |
| `internal/migrations` | embedded goose SQL migrations |
| `core/<entity>` | domain business logic + Postgres store |
| `api/<entity>` | REST transport (typed handlers) |

Add a domain module with `skit add rest <name>`, then wire its store/core/handler
in `internal/app/deps` and its routes in `internal/app/server`.
